# UX Standards

Yowl is a Slack-baseline utility chat: snappy, device-appropriate, lovable
because it works. Full rationale in [`docs/ux.md`](../../docs/ux.md).

## SuperAdmin tools

- UI gates (`isSuperAdminPhone`) are **UX only** — pair every privileged action
  with SQL `is_superadmin()` RLS, security-definer RPCs, and Edge checks
  (`get_site_lockdown` / `is_superadmin_phone` on auth OTP; skip
  `user_moderation.super_banned_at` recipients in notify).
- **Two group soft-state axes — do not conflate:** `deleted_at` = creator
  soft-delete (reversible); `deactivated_at` = SuperAdmin moderation. Never use
  hard `DELETE` for rooms from the client.
- Lockdown: signed-out OTP only via `/superadmin`; Edge rejects non-SuperAdmin
  phones while `site_settings.lockdown` is true. Precedence: lockdown →
  super-ban → app. `AppLayout` must **hold** on `useAuthState` loading (and
  moderation when signed in) — do not treat `user: null` as non-admin. Do
  **not** hold on `useSiteSettings` loading: that query hangs with no network
  and leaves the offline PWA shell on `site-gate-loading` instead of
  `sign-in-screen`. Apply lockdown only when settings data is present; on
  settings error, fail open (Edge still blocks OTP). Symptom → check:
  SuperAdmin briefly sees site-offline; super-banned sees chrome first; or
  `offline-shell` e2e times out waiting for `sign-in-screen`.
- Admin chat posts: `messages.is_admin_message` + SuperAdmin insert RLS (no
  membership). Display as **Yowl Admin**, non-interactive; self-only
  “Posting as system admin” banner.
- E2E: `seedSuperAdminSession` + `tests/e2e/superadmin.spec.ts` (incl. suggestion **Create GitHub issue** visibility).
- **`useAuthState` is per-mount local state** (starts `user: null`,
  `loading: true`). Nested children that remount under `RequireAuth` must not
  call `useAuthState` again and non-null-assert `user!.uid` — back-navigation
  can paint warm TanStack Query rows while the child’s session is still null
  (`Cannot read properties of null (reading 'uid')`). Pass `AppUser` from the
  parent that already resolved auth, and wait on `loading` before SuperAdmin
  deny screens. Symptom → check: crash on admin list remount / back.

## Color roles (never mix)

- **Purple = brand/neutral foundation** — the `gray` scale is purple-tinted;
  `brand.*` for identity moments and selected nav (`nav.selected`)
- **Teal = action** — `action.*` / `preset="primary"` for buttons, links,
  switches, focus rings. Only on things the user can do
- **Status stays semantic** — green success, red error/destructive, amber
  warning, blue info. Never use purple/teal for status, or status hues for chrome
- Use semantic tokens (`surface.canvas|raised|sunken`, `border.subtle`,
  `text.muted`) — not raw hex or component-local colors

## Layout contract

- App frame is fixed-viewport (`AppLayout` in `src/components/AppShell.tsx`):
  desktop (md+) = persistent sidebar (brand + plus at top; user + appearance
  in the footer); mobile
  = compact header, room pages render their own single top bar. Document
  does not scroll — pages scroll internally (`flex={1} minH={0} overflowY="auto"`)
- **Predictable chrome:** for fixed-size shells (room header, composer, sidebar
  width), mount the container at its known dimensions immediately, then fill
  contents when data is ready — never omit the frame until load completes
  (avoids pop-in). Skeletons go *inside* the frame.
- Chat: chronological messages, composer pinned to bottom, Enter sends
  (Shift+Enter newline), optimistic pending bubbles
- Overlays: small menus/popovers → `MorphingPopover` (9-point overlapping
  `anchor`, default `center`, then viewport clamp); larger forms/listings →
  `QuickModal` (modal on md+, tray/drawer on mobile). Tray placement follows
  the trigger (top chrome → top tray; bottom chrome → bottom tray)

## Focus-gated chrome and nested overlays

When visibility depends on focus or keyboard state (common on mobile — e.g.
composer format toolbar only while the editor is focused):

- **Pin chrome while a child overlay is open.** Any `MorphingPopover`,
  `QuickModal`, or `autoFocus` field inside focus-gated markup blurs the
  parent on open → the parent unmounts → the popover disappears before the
  user can type. Include overlay open state in the gate:
  `showChrome = !isMobile || focused || overlayOpen` (see
  `RichTextEditor.tsx` link URL popover + `linkOpen`).
- **Keep persistent actions outside the collapsing strip.** Affordances that
  must stay visible when the strip hides (Send) → absolutely position over the
  editor; only the format row collapses.
- **Pre-ship:** mobile viewport → open nested popover → **type and paste**
  into its input in the same PR (Playwright or manual). Desktop-only checks
  miss this class of bug.

## Native / PWA

- **Viewport:** see `docs/ux.md` (anti-patterns table). Short version: browser
  `#root` `inset: 0`; iOS standalone `#root { height: 100vh }` (not
  `bottom:0`/`dvh`). Keyboard open only when VV shrinks **and** editable focused.
  Closed: composer pads safe-area once. Never VV-size `#root` while closed; wipe
  webclip Storage after `index.html` changes; verify bottom gap with pixels
- **First paint:** `index.html` sets `color-scheme` (`dark light`), dark-first
  raised CSS on `html`/`body`, canvas on `#root`, and an early body script
  (Chakra mode + those bgs) so the UA never flashes white before React. Do not
  put `ColorModeScript` only inside React.
- **Color mode persistence:** `initialColorMode: 'system'` is fine for first
  visit; keep `useSystemColorMode: false`. Live system sync overwrites
  `chakra-ui-color-mode` when iOS Automatic (or any OS schedule) flips —
  in-app dark mode is “forgotten” ~daily. Guard with `theme-modes` e2e
  (`page.emulateMedia` after seeding dark). See [`docs/ux.md`](../../docs/ux.md).
- **Document vs content:** `html`/`body`/`theme-color` = `surface.raised`
  (matches composer; iOS Safari accessory bar samples document bg). `#root` /
  AppShell = `surface.canvas`. Do not paint document with canvas.
- **Edges:** pad chrome with `env(safe-area-inset-*)` (no body+shell
  double-subtract). `theme-color` + manifest colors track raised (incl. in-app
  color-mode sync); `apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style` =
  `black-translucent` when edge-to-edge
- **Overlays:** QuickModal has X (and/or Cancel). MorphingPopover dismisses via
  Esc / outside click; Close is optional (`showClose`). **Small** (menus,
  short action lists, popovers) → `MorphingPopover` (overlapping `anchor` +
  viewport clamp with safe-area). **Large** (forms, listings, multi-field
  content) → `QuickModal` tray/modal (top below `md`, centered from `md` up,
  ≥16px from edges); confirmations use the same mobile drawer shell.
  Tray placement: top chrome → top tray; bottom chrome → bottom tray.
  Morphing spring counts in the micro-motion budget (~≤400ms); honor
  `prefers-reduced-motion`. Overlay focus rings use `_focusVisible` so
  programmatic open focus does not glow.
- **Menus:** prefer `MorphingPopover` for short action lists on all
  viewports (Account, room title, message author). Use `PopoverMenuRow`
  (fixed-width icon column + FontAwesome `fixedWidth`) so labels align.
  Longer navigational lists (rooms) may still use a floating drawer. Legacy
  `ActionSheet` / `Menu` only until migrated

## States — never blank

- No `if (error) return null` — use `UI.ErrorState` (with retry) or a toast
- No empty `return null` for lists — use `UI.EmptyState` with a CTA
- Loading: `Skeleton` matching final layout, not bare full-screen spinners
- Submits: button `isLoading` + double-submit guard; failed sends restore input
- **Toggle / vote controls:** do not call the API with prop state that only
  updates after a list refetch (`votedByMe`, switch checked, etc.). Keep
  optimistic local state (or keep `isLoading` until the parent value matches
  the mutation). Otherwise a second tap races the refetch and double-inserts /
  shows a spurious error. Revert local state on failure. Reference:
  `SuggestionRow` in `SuggestionsPage.tsx`. Message reactions use the same
  pattern via cache `applyReactionInsert` / `applyReactionDelete` before the
  network call (`MessageReactionsBar`).

## Message reactions

- Fixed allow-list only (`REACTION_EMOJIS` in `src/lib/chat/reactionEmojis.ts`).
  Keep the Postgres `message_reactions_emoji_allowed` CHECK in sync when the
  set changes — do not invent a free-text emoji column.
- **List vs detail:** In the chat list, show the smile Add control only when the
  message already has reaction chips (trailing the chip row). First reaction
  comes from tap/hover on the message body → `QuickModal` ("Message") which
  always shows Add (`alwaysShowAdd`). Picker MorphingPopover has no title —
  use `aria-label="Add reaction"` only. Pending/failed outbox rows hide the bar
  and cannot open detail.
- Symptom → check: Preview toast *Couldn't update reaction* with a working
  local e2e → `message_reactions` missing on **quacker-dev**; `supabase db push`
  that migration before Preview smoke.

Prefer foolproof entry over free-text + late validation:

- **Masked** for fixed formats (phone → `UI.MaskedInput` + `react-hook-mask`;
  see `subtypeMetas`)
- **Typed / filtered** for constrained char sets (display name → letters +
  spaces only)
- **Hard limits** via `maxLength`, TipTap `CharacterCount`, or Zod — show a
  counter when the limit matters (e.g. message `n/140`)
- **Purpose-built controls** when they improve a11y and reduce errors:
  OTP → `PinInput` (one field per digit); picks from a set → combobox /
  select, not a free text box; dates/money → existing form subtype inputs.
  For wrapped OTP (`VerificationCodeInput`): call `onComplete` from **one**
  path only — either Chakra `PinInput`’s `onComplete` **or** your
  `onChange`/`applyValue` when `digits.length === length`, never both
  (double submit / double verify)
- **Single-field rename/prompt modals** (change name, rename room): keep the
  dialog narrow (`QuickModal` `size="sm"`) and put an **inset Save icon
  button** in the input (`InputGroup` + `InputRightElement`) — not a
  full-width footer primary
- **Password managers:** `@@ui` `Input` / `MaskedInput` default to
  `passwordManagerIgnoreProps` (1Password / LastPass / Bitwarden / Dashlane).
  Do **not** rely on `autoComplete="off"` alone. Set semantic
  `autoComplete` when it helps (`nickname`, `tel`, `one-time-code`) and
  only pass `allowPasswordManager` on real credential fields (sign-in
  phone). Never disable managers on authentic login/OTP entry.

Plain `UI.Input` is fine for truly open text. Do not invent a new mask library
when `MaskedInput` / form subtypes already cover the case.

## Product rules

- Room lists are **membership-scoped** (`useGroups({ userId })`) — never list
  all rooms
- Joining is **explicit consent** (join prompt), never a silent side effect
- Ask for a display name right after first sign-in (**What's your name?**);
  `···1234` is a fallback, not an identity. Organic FTUE then offers create-room
  (Skip allowed); invite links skip create and go to the room
- Destructive actions (leave/delete/ban) go through `useConfirmation` with
  `isDestructive: true`; never confirm create/send

## Motion budget

2–3 intentional micro-motions only (message appear ~160ms, pressed-state
translate, MorphingPopover spring ≤ ~400ms, Chakra modal/drawer defaults).
Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. No decorative animation, gradients, or gloss.

## Copy

- **Sentence case** for UI labels, titles, and buttons (e.g. "Room options",
  "Invite someone") — not Title Case. Brand **Yowl** stays capitalized.
- User-facing strings say **Yowl** (capital Y), never Quacker and never
  lowercase **yowl** as brand text; no developer copy in error screens (no
  "Vite", "dev server")
- Brand chrome: signed-in header logo opens an about popover; accessible name is
  **Yowl** (`getByRole('button', { name: 'Yowl' })`). Logged-out / FTUE: large
  logo image (`sign-in-logo`), no header brand button
- When changing labels, dialog titles, `aria-label`s, or adding a second control
  with the same accessible name, update Playwright / Maestro selectors **in the
  same change** (see playwright-chrome rule)
- Errors are human + actionable ("Check your connection and try again.")
